.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
.Dd October 15, 2026
.Dt IPCRM 1
.Os OxideBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm ipcrm
.Nd remove System V message queues, semaphore sets and shared memory segments
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl vW
.Op Fl q Ar msqid
.Op Fl m Ar shmid
.Op Fl s Ar semid
.Op Fl Q Ar msgkey
.Op Fl M Ar shmkey
.Op Fl S Ar semkey
.Ar ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
removes the objects it is given, by identifier or by key:
.Bl -tag -width "-Q msgkey"
.It Fl q Ar msqid
the message queue
.Ar msqid ;
.It Fl m Ar shmid
the shared memory segment
.Ar shmid ;
.It Fl s Ar semid
the semaphore set
.Ar semid ;
.It Fl Q Ar msgkey
the message queue with key
.Ar msgkey ;
.It Fl M Ar shmkey
the shared memory segment with key
.Ar shmkey ;
.It Fl S Ar semkey
the semaphore set with key
.Ar semkey .
.El
.Pp
An identifier of \-1 stands for every object of its kind,
.Fl W
for every object of every kind.
Numbers may be decimal, or hexadecimal or octal with C's prefixes.
.Fl v
reports each object removed.
.Pp
Removing an object needs its owner, its creator or the superuser.
A shared memory segment still attached is removed once the last process
detaches it; its key is free at once.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ipcs 1 ,
.Xr msgctl 2 ,
.Xr semctl 2 ,
.Xr shmctl 2
.Sh STANDARDS
.Nm
is in the X/Open System Interfaces option of
.St -p1003.1-2008 .
.Fl v , W
and an identifier of \-1 are extensions, from
.Fx .
.Sh HISTORY
.Nm
appeared in AT&T System V.
OxideBSD's first appeared in 0.3.0, replacing BusyBox's.
